## Summary

One blocking finding. The GitHub deploy identity holds project-level editor, run.admin,
storage.admin, and iam.serviceAccountUser in www-reading-advantage. That is a no-build path, so
the PM acceptance does not bound it. The 2.6 grants in primary-advantage and reading-advantage are
least-privileged for a build submit. Both CD workflows hold contents: read only, use exactly the two
existing secrets, echo no secret, and take no untrusted input into a shell line. No workflow moves
traffic. The primary, accounts, and marketing traffic files require _TAG with no default. The
workbooks job fails closed. A2 is not applicable. A6 holds.

