## Blocking

B1 (owner: PM; Daniel decides; not a Green code change). The identity
www-reading-github@www-reading-advantage (the GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT key that both CD workflows use)
holds project-level roles/editor, roles/run.admin, roles/storage.admin, and
roles/iam.serviceAccountUser in project www-reading-advantage. A key holder can deploy or delete
the www-reading-advantage service and move its traffic with no build, and can act as any service
account in that project. The PM acceptance covers build accounts in primary-advantage and
reading-advantage only. Task 4.7 (WIF plus key deletion) does not remove these grants. Recommended
fix: reduce the identity to cloudbuild.builds.editor, serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer,
logging.viewer, run.viewer, and objectCreator/objectViewer on www-reading-advantage_cloudbuild;
remove editor, run.admin, storage.admin, and serviceAccountUser; add the reduction to task 4.7.
The grant is pre-existing. It is confined to the www project; the identity has no run role in
primary-advantage or reading-advantage.

## Nonblocking

N1 (PM and track owner, task 2.3h): accounting, codecamp-advantage, and sales-advantage move
traffic to a fixed tag name. Spec section 2a and the runbook document the tag. Sales takes
_PUSH_BUILD_ID for the rollback capture but its traffic move ignores it, so the capture and the
target can name different builds.

N2 (task 4.7): the PM accepted the default build account. Measured: primary-advantage uses
1064299189080-compute@developer (editor, run.admin, actAs, secretAccessor); reading-advantage uses
1090865515742@cloudbuild (run.admin, actAs, no editor).

N3 (task 4.7): project-level logging.viewer and storage.bucketViewer are broader than a build submit
needs.

N4 (PM, design note): a tagged revision of a service with --allow-unauthenticated is publicly
reachable at its tag URL. --no-traffic is not an access gate.

N5 (track owner): the workflows use mutable major tags (@v4, @v2), not commit SHAs.

N6 (task 2.3i): workbooks-cloud-run holds only cloudsql.client. It also needs
secretmanager.secretAccessor on the two future WORKBOOKS_* secrets.

N7 (track owner): measure/tracks.md still says the track status is "Phase 1 (affected-app logic)
next". The line is stale. It is not a security overstatement.

## Evidence

- Permissions: both CD workflows declare permissions: contents: read exactly. No id-token, no
  pull_request_target, no write-all, no pull_request trigger. The repository default workflow
  permission is read.
- Secrets: only GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT and GCP_PROJECT_ID appear in .github/workflows. gh secret list
  returns exactly those two, both created 2026-05-23. No echo of a secret; no set -x, no
  printenv, no env pipe.
- Injection: github.event.before and github.sha pass through env and are quoted. The matrix is
  JSON-encoded, so no GITHUB_OUTPUT line split. matrix values come from scripts/ci/apps.json, not
  from a branch name, a commit message, or a PR title.
- Traffic: git grep for update-traffic, --to-latest, and cloudbuild-traffic over
  .github/workflows exits 1. The update-traffic steps use --to-tags only. primary, accounts, and
  marketing require ${_TAG} with no default. sales requires ${_PUSH_BUILD_ID} with no default.
- IAM (primary-advantage and reading-advantage): the member holds only cloudbuild.builds.editor,
  logging.viewer, serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer, and storage.bucketViewer. No owner, editor,
  or *.admin role.
- Buckets (primary-advantage_cloudbuild, reading-advantage_cloudbuild): objectCreator and
  objectViewer only. No delete role.
- Keys: two system-managed keys and one user-managed key. The user-managed key dates from
  2026-05-23. Task 2.6 made no key.
- www-reading-advantage: editor, iam.serviceAccountUser, run.admin, storage.admin for the member.
  One service and one build bucket in the project.
- Workbooks fails closed: no workbooks repo, no workbooks service, no WORKBOOKS_* secret.
- Secrets in Cloud Build: secrets mount only through secretEnv and availableSecrets. The Cloud
  Build service account is secretAccessor on COMPANY_AUTH_DIRECT_DATABASE_URL.
- Error handling: every bash step starts with set -euo pipefail.
- No credential in the diff. Only scripts/ci/apps.json matches a key or secret file name.
- No workflow run: gh run list shows only old www and CI runs. "CD - gated apps" never ran.
- A2 not applicable. A6 holds.

